part.think:
So there's no public cpSpace getter. However, `cpBodyGetSpace(body)` is a Chipmunk API that returns the cpSpace a body is in (or NULL). I could obtain the space lazily from any body in the world. But fragile if no bodies.

Decision: implement init to store _world, and attempt to resolve _space lazily via a helper that scans `world->getAllBodies()` for a body whose cpBodyGetSpace returns non-null. If no space can be resolved, fall back to PhysicsWorld::rayCast public API? That adds complexity.

Hmm wait — actually, let me reconsider. Is cpBodyGetSpace reliable? Bodies added via addBodyOrDelay: bodies might be in _delayAddBodies and not yet in space; cpBodyGetSpace returns NULL then. But getAllBodies() returns _bodies which contains bodies after updateBodies... Actually in upstream, addBodyOrDelay checks `cpSpaceContainsBody`? Let me recall upstream addBody: if body's world set... _bodies.pushBack in doAddBody. getAllBodies returns _bodies. Bodies in _bodies are in the space (doAddBody calls cpSpaceAddBody only for dynamic? In upstream cocos2d-x, doAddBody: `if (body->_dynamic) { cpSpaceAddBody(_cpSpace, body->_cpBody); }` — static/kinematic bodies are NOT added to the space! So cpBodyGetSpace returns NULL for them.

Hmm. This lazy approach is genuinely fragile.

Better: use PhysicsWorld::rayCast public API for segment queries. It's the natural path: benchmark restored CCPhysicsWorld will implement rayCast with cpSpaceSegmentQuery. The info struct PhysicsRayCastInfo gives shape, contact, normal, fraction. Everything I need for RayCastHit: shape, body (shape->getBody()), point=contact, normal, fraction, distance = fraction * segmentLength.

Filtering: I need categoryMask/collisionMask/group filtering. PhysicsWorld::rayCast uses CP_SHAPE_FILTER_ALL so it reports everything; I filter manually:

```cpp
static bool shapePassesFilter(cpShape* shape, unsigned int categoryMask, unsigned int collisionMask, int group)
{
    cpShapeFilter f = cpShapeGetFilter(shape);
    if (group != 0 && f.group == (cpGroup)group) return false;
    if ((f.categories & collisionMask) == 0) return false;
    if ((f.mask & categoryMask) == 0) return false;
    return true;
